A||||7||sloth85GT||Failed attempt at white lenses for coupe......||||8||
Z||000000||sloth85GT||10-14-2001||12:31 AM||||As the subject says, I was bored today, so I went down to Revy and picked up some of that white Flourescent light cover plastic, made a template out of paper that fit inside of my old tail light cover, then cut out a piece of that plastic stuff to fit with the Dremel. Where I went wrong was shaping it. I used the heat gun a little TOO much and warped it to hell. I also didn't take into account that plastic shrinks when heated. So that's attempt number one. If anyone has any ideas on how I can go about this a little better, please let me hear them, I'm all ears.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||8
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-14-2001||04:02 PM||||I haven't actually worked on a coupe taillight yet... but I didn't think that they needed to be flexed?  Just cut to size & shape and glued/siliconed in place...?  I guess I'll have to go take a look at one later (got one in the garage waiting for the white lens).  I'll let you know if I come up with anything specific!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||85 gt fiero||10-14-2001||04:28 PM||||are you talking about clear tailights because you can just take out the honeycombs and wahla. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||10-14-2001||04:30 PM||||You only get the 5hp bonus if it's MOULDED  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>J/k....<P>Have a little experience with plastic like that. What are you using to heat it? If it's a paint-stripper style heater, don't hold it closer than 12" and don't melt the plastic. Keep constant force over the mandrel while you heat.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||10-14-2001||04:31 PM||||Just putting in colored bulbs without the reflectors/diffusers would be illegal in some places, that's why many of the import tail lights were recalled and replaced... I think it needs a diffuser to be legal.. plus it looks better..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 10-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||sloth85GT||10-14-2001||06:28 PM||||well it doesn't really need to be flexed, it just fits a little better that way. I don't really plan on using these on my car, who knows, when I make a set, I'll test fit it on my car, maybe it'll look good. I was just bored. Maybe next weekend I will try again when I have time. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||qwikgta||10-15-2001||10:05 PM||||Dan,<BR>  When I did mine, I didn't heat the plastic, I just cut it a little big and then kept cutting it down until it fit the way I wanted it to.  Im happy with mine but I think I got lucky.  Good luck.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 66K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, GT rear swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails, KYB's, dropped springs.<P>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject/robsfieroproject.html<BR>   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||sloth85GT||10-16-2001||02:26 AM||||I think I went a little overboard with the heating, I thought it would be easier and I wanted it to be perfect. Do you have any pics of yours qwikgta?||||reg||1
